#
# Reference: https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#trivyignore
#
# One vulnerability, misconfiguration, or secret rule ID per line.
# A line starting with # is a comment and suppresses nothing. Remove the
# leading # to activate an example:
#
#   CVE-2019-14697 exp:2027-01-01
#   AVD-DS-0002
#   generic-unwanted-rule
#
# `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` limits a suppression to that date. After it, trivy
# reports the finding again.
#
# This file sits beside the configured trivy.yml, so the scan uses it.
# A .trivyignore at the repository root applies only when this file is
# absent; the two are never merged.
